cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "LAPLACE prototype: a closed discovery loop on a networked physical system"
abstract: >-
  A feasibility prototype of a full scientific-discovery loop on a simulated
  118-bus transmission network: a graph world model with deep-ensemble
  epistemic uncertainty, curiosity-driven intervention under a hard voltage
  envelope, and sparse symbolic distillation of the active-power flow equation,
  scored against the simulator's known admittance matrix.
authors:
  - family-names: Araar
    given-names: Sarra
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-22"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - active learning
  - world models
  - symbolic regression
  - uncertainty quantification
  - power systems
